@startuml UiOutputVocabulary
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: the fixed status vocabulary proveo prints, and why it degrades rather than decorates
' covers: internal/ui/**
title Output vocabulary — one printer, five verbs, two renderings

component "Printer{W, Plain}\nline(icon, tag, format)" as P <<app>>
component "Okf · Warnf · Failf\nNotef · Iconf" as VERBS <<app>>
component "isFancy(w)\nTTY probe" as FANCY <<app>>
component "stripANSI" as STRIP <<app>>
component "Default → os.Stderr" as DEF <<app>>
component "TeeTo(w)\nrun log" as TEE <<app>>
database "terminal\n✓ · ⚠️ · ❌ · 📦" as TERM <<db>>
database "log file / pipe\nok: · warn: · error:" as LOG <<db>>

VERBS ARROW_MAIN P
P ARROW_MAIN FANCY : which rendering
FANCY ARROW_MAIN TERM : fancy
FANCY ARROW_QUEUE LOG : plain
DEF ARROW_MAIN P
TEE ARROW_MAIN STRIP
STRIP ARROW_MAIN LOG

note right of VERBS
  **A fixed vocabulary, not free-form printing.** Every status line proveo
  emits goes through one of five verbs, so the shape of output is a property of
  the package rather than of each call site. ""Notef"" carries no prefix in
  either rendering — it is the continuation line under a preceding verb, which
  is how a warning attaches its detail without repeating the marker.
end note

note bottom of FANCY
  **Plain is a degradation, never a second design.** The same call renders
  ""✓ added /bin to PATH"" on a terminal and ""ok: added /bin to PATH"" elsewhere:
  the icon is replaced by a word, never dropped, so a grep over a log finds the
  same events a human read on screen. ""Iconf"" is the one exception — its icon
  is decoration attached to an already-complete sentence, so plain mode drops
  it rather than inventing a tag for it.
end note

note bottom of STRIP
  **The tee strips ANSI on the way to the log, not at the source.** Colour is
  chosen once for the terminal; the log copy is sanitised as it is written, so
  a run transcript stays greppable without the print sites having to know a
  file is listening. See ""_spec/internal/runlog/run-transcript\.puml"".
end note

note bottom of DEF
  **Status goes to stderr so stdout stays machine-clean.** A caller piping
  ""proveo run --print"" gets argv and nothing else; the narration lands beside
  it on the other stream.
end note

@enduml
